 "pairs": [],
 "limits": [
  "a folded value proves the string the source would build at that point; it does not prove the call that consumes it resolves a module object, so a folded import-string route is a route and not a demonstration",
  "operands are resolved from module-scope assignments and from assignments inside the enclosing function, taking the first assignment in source order; a name reassigned before the site is published with its assignment count but not ordered, which is a limit of the resolver rather than a claim about the value",
  "a name bound by a loop or comprehension target is not resolved even when the iterable is a literal list of strings, because the value depends on the iteration the string is built in; those sites are published as residual with their binding class",
  "conversion (!r / !s) and a format spec inside an f-string are not folded; the site is published with that reason so the evasion is visible",
  "templates are matched as whole tokens with E647's match classes, so a fragment that names only a family prefix is not a hit",
  "the read population is E638's join (one definition), so a change to that join moves this study's pairs without touching its sites",
  "files over 1MB are skipped rather than parsed (E391's cap) and are counted by the population this study re-derives"
